{
 "id": "argonia-flora-provisional-v1",
 "status": "PROVISIONAL \u2014 densities, species mix and scale ranges are the phase agent's proposal, pending the owner's placement decisions (see docs/world/decisions pack in PROGRESS). The machinery is not provisional; these numbers are.",
 "grounding": {
  "canonFlora": "world/sources/lore/topics/fauna-hazards.md \u00a7 Flora \u2014 CANON_EXPLICIT: cypress, mangrove (a ten-mile wall near Lilmoth), bamboo, sleeping palms, palm, bog willow, flint vine, dragon's-tongue, nightbloom, somnalius fern, marshweed, blue moss canopies, fields of ferns and flowered grasses, lucan mold, starblossom, toxicodor, nirnroot",
  "gradient": "world/sources/lore/black-marsh-province.md: temperate grassland north-east -> rainforest and drowned coast south",
  "minedRules": "docs/research/shipped-world-placement-rules.md \u2014 R1 clumping, R2 waterline density peak, R3 slope falloff, R4 flooding classes, R5/R6 palette breadth and region contrast, R7 guilds",
  "regionClasses": "tooling/world-generation/worldgen/regions.py REGION_CLASSES"
 },
 "conventions": {
  "water_depth_m": "hard gate on standing water over the ground: positive is flooded, negative is height above the local water table",
  "scale_range": "multiplier on the source mesh's native size. The source pools are deliberately oversized (a 32 m cypress at 1.0); staying near 1.0 is a decision, not a default",
  "tier": "T1 hero placed statics, T2 instanced mid detail. Groundcover is not here \u2014 it is groundcover.json, keyed on land cover like Bethesda's LTEX->GRAS binding",
  "instances_per_hectare": "instances per hectare of ideal ground, before the depth and slope responses thin them \u2014 the same unit the mining measured, so a number here can be read straight against docs/research/shipped-world-placement-rules.md",
  "clumping": "clump_size_median / clump_radius_m / singleton_share shape the clustering; the defaults are calibrated to Clark-Evans R 0.5-0.6 against the mined 0.45",
  "depth_response": "depth_half_width_m defaults to 0 = flat inside the gate; only water-edge species set a peak and a width",
  "densityScale": "global multiplier over every layer, so 'how dense should Argonia feel' is one owner decision rather than sixty numbers",
  "landmarkGiants": "Layers tagged role=landmark-giant are the owner's 0036 Q2 choice: the ordinary canopy sits near native scale and a few giants (x1.8-2.6, so 58-83 m on a 32 m cypress) stand out to navigate by. They are placed for visibility rather than cover \u2014 roughly one per 8-16 ha \u2014 take no notice of clearance themselves, and stamp a wide clearance so nothing crowds the silhouette. Their density is additive to the climate-derived target, which it barely moves."
 },
