 "densityScale": 1.0,
 "densityModel": {
  "formula": "instances/ha = 850 * humidity^2 * (0.25 + 0.75 * canopy)",
  "why": "The ladder falls out of the province's own climate fields (regions.CLIMATE) rather than being asserted per region: water availability dominates in a swamp, canopy closure carries the rest, and bare ground still gets scrub off the 0.25 floor. BASE is set so the province-wide mean lands near the reference mod's dressed median of ~100/ha (the owner's 'matches the reference' choice, 2026-08-30) while the ladder spreads about 12x from jungle to bare mountain. Evidence and the three inputs behind it: docs/research/vegetation-density-design.md",
  "variation": "Per-region targets are the MEAN. Within a region the shared openness field and per-species patchiness reproduce the reference's coefficient of variation (2.3-3.1x) at its measured wavelengths (~90 m glades, ~190 m stands).",
  "calibration": "BASE was raised from 250 to 850 against the one statistic measured identically on both sides: median open-space radius between plants. The reference mod sits at 10.2 m; at BASE 250 the compiler produced 18.9 m, and open space scales as 1/sqrt(density). Re-measure with `compile_scatter --report` after any change to the region raster."
 }
}
